<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>My Father’s own Son, the Savior of men,</l><l>Once wandered on earth as the poorest of them.</l><l>But now He is pleading our pardon on high,</l><l>That we may be His when He comes by and by.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>I once was an out-cast stranger on earth,</l><l>A sinner by choice, and an alien by birth;</l><l>But I’ve been adopted, my name’s written down,</l><l>An heir of salvation, the kingdom and crown.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>Though poor on this earth, oh, why should I care?</l><l>Since glorious things for me God doth prepare;</l><l>Though trials abound, yet, still I may sing:</l><l>All glory to God, I’m a child of the King.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
